# physics_baseline.scene
# Comprehensive physics baseline: captures full ball state (position, velocity, omega)
# for a fixed set of configurations to regression-test physics behavior.
# Run in Debug build via --scene; output goes to Debug/physics_state.csv.
#
# Configurations tested:
#   1. drop_flat   — Ball dropped vertically onto flat terrain (bounce + settle)
#   2. roll_slope  — Ball placed on slope, rolls downhill under gravity
#   3. roll_flat   — Ball given initial velocity on flat terrain (deceleration test)
#   4. collide_a/b — Two balls aimed at each other for collision response

physics on
text off
frames 600
fixed_step

# Elevated camera looking down at the scene
camera overview 500 200 500  500 50 500  0 1 0

# Ball 1: drop_flat — dropped from height onto relatively flat terrain (center of map)
ball drop_flat 500 120 500  8.0 30.0 15.0 0.6  0 0 0  0 0 0

# Ball 2: roll_slope — placed on the terrain slope with an initial push downhill
ball roll_slope 700 100 500  8.0 30.0 15.0 0.3  -400 0 0  0 0 0

# Ball 3: roll_flat — placed on relatively flat terrain with horizontal velocity
ball roll_flat 500 80 700  8.0 30.0 15.0 0.3  0 0 -300  0 0 0

# Ball 4+5: collide_a and collide_b — converging for a head-on collision
ball collide_a 400 80 400  8.0 30.0 15.0 0.5  300 0 0  0 0 0
ball collide_b 600 80 400  8.0 30.0 15.0 0.5  -300 0 0  0 0 0
